{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development has failed to provide any affordable housing. The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-Chpater 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policies H4 and H5 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DHM1 of the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposal has failed to provide adequate and functional&nbsp;private and communal external amenity space for all of the units, thus represents a poorly designed development with inadequate quality of accommodation.&nbsp;The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-Policy D6 and&nbsp;S4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMNE 1 the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The bulk and mass of the proposed development would present a overly prominent building, with a fragmented roofline with a height significantly greater than the other buildings in the area. The proposal has also failed to&nbsp;contribute to enhancing the provision of greening on the site. This represents poor quality design and would cause harm to the character of the site and surrounding area, notably since its location within the Becontree Estate.&nbsp;The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-Paragraphs 131, 135 and 203 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policies D4 and&nbsp;HC1&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies CP3 and&nbsp;CP2&nbsp;of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies BP11 and BP2 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies DMD1, DMD4, and SPP6 of the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposal has failed to submit a daylight/sunlight report and adequately&nbsp;demonstrate that the proposed development would not cause any additional loss of daylight, privacy, outlook nor cause additional overshadowing or an overbearing impact to neighbouring properties.&nbsp;The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policy BP8 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policy DMD1 of the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposal has failed to submit a transport assessment thus has not demonstrated trips generated nor a clear car parking arrangement.&nbsp;The acceptability of these matters therefore cannot be assessed&nbsp;adequately.&nbsp;The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-Chapter 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policy T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy&nbsp;BR11&nbsp;the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policy DMT 2 the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposal has failed to&nbsp;adeqautely indicate&nbsp;the proposed refuse and recycling provision nor submit a refuse and recycling strategy, resulting in the inability to effectively assess the impact of the proposed development.The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:-Policy DMSI 8&nbsp;the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021).The&nbsp;Council&#39;s Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments (dated&nbsp;20/05/2021)&nbsp;"
  ],
